        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where DeepInfra video generation requests did not apply the configured provider request policy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe DeepInfra video generation path now passes the sanitized provider request policy into its HTTP resolver, allowing custom headers, dispatcher policy, and private-network behavior to reach the actual generation request. The change does not modify model selection, provider parameters, or response parsing.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted contribution prepared for Alix-007.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators using DeepInfra video generation get consistent request-policy behavior with the rest of the provider stack, including expected proxy/header/network controls.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/deepinfra/video-generation-provider.test.ts`\n- Result: 1 test file passed, 10 tests passed.\n- `git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD --`\n- Result: passed.\n",
